{"id": "EUVD-2026-76653", "enisaUuid": "9baee555-ac09-396b-8285-75d8decd6d72", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRevert \"media: v4l2-dev: fix error handling in __video_register_device()\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2a934fdb01db6458288fc9386d3d8ceba6dd551a.\n\nThe intentions of that patch were good, but it doesn't work.\n\nThe idea is that if device_register fails, you have to do a put_device\nto let the ref counter release resources.\n\nHowever, the V4L2 API says that if video_register_device() fails, then\nyou have to call video_device_release(), which kfree()s the video_device\nstruct.\n\nBut the put_device() will already have freed the struct, so you end\nup in a double-free scenario.\n\nThere is not really a good way of fixing this without breaking\nvideo_register_device() into two parts, one that initializes everything,\nand one that does the actual device_register, and then converting all\nV4L2 drivers to this new model.\n\nThat is a massive job, and it is very unlikely that device_register\nwill fail.\n\nSo rather than ending up in a double-free scenario, just revert this\npatch, and in that case we'll have a small memory leak. Which is a lot\nmore robust.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:55", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b998c171ed875e402e1fd1c5cd619e4ca05e9c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3de14b4f681a1b3c6d375d98d9d37a55ebb85349", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8027f82c0f5474ed72448e160ee9778051fa1f49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ac009a65d2385e9f0799eaf9d9694a29153a161", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/712ca1cf756de2557a116e0df55791bac0c9f99e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aad08b5f67d2a8116e1a00bce2611c1513b10bce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce792b94e03882108019ba996c1a7c4d4e09be2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7600f5cee5de14065f950807931d6e6d40fb2d7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89741", "GHSA-x4c4-qfr2-c3vv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "073f3889-b94d-3f7a-9240-384a42adc1fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2429bb9fad88c8fa84c4956b0a21cf5afe5e92b7 <712ca1cf756de2557a116e0df55791bac0c9f99e"}, {"id": "080b708a-8114-3ea3-b1af-4ee1e54b9509", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ee141706e701356dda41c6fed9ee18bf427c28e3"}, {"id": "08c70912-6844-39ec-8b73-9b9fe6249173", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae7b143e05b36fc69d6571751855946cc45064c6 <2ac009a65d2385e9f0799eaf9d9694a29153a161"}, {"id": "0b905f09-070f-3280-861f-da9240397fee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2a934fdb01db6458288fc9386d3d8ceba6dd551a <ce792b94e03882108019ba996c1a7c4d4e09be2c"}, {"id": "19228dad-ab2c-32fb-ad77-289199edb10c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "2736783d-0ee3-3e59-860e-a81743321301", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "28833a4b-8077-309b-9825-c97303814d46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2a934fdb01db6458288fc9386d3d8ceba6dd551a <e7600f5cee5de14065f950807931d6e6d40fb2d7"}, {"id": "28f9d9b9-90b0-366a-a7c8-f0817209341e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2a934fdb01db6458288fc9386d3d8ceba6dd551a <aad08b5f67d2a8116e1a00bce2611c1513b10bce"}, {"id": "2e185033-f5e8-3bff-bc7e-f72570cccd1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b451a9a46f2bfc510e6d5c2492df91647586184 <3de14b4f681a1b3c6d375d98d9d37a55ebb85349"}, {"id": "32125122-d808-3fdb-9593-0268504a38ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":